.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES ASA SHUN ADD" "1" "2026-09-02" "0.41.0" "sccfm-cli inventory devices asa shun add Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-asa\-shun\-add \- Shun (block) one or more source IP...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices asa shun add
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shun (block) one or more source IP addresses on ASA devices. Each --source-ip can carry an inline connection tuple as: '<src_ip> [<dst_ip> [<src_port> [<dst_port> [<protocol>]]]]'. For a single entry, the tuple fields can also be passed as separate --dest-ip / --source-port / --dest-port / --protocol flags.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-device\-name TEXT
Device name to search for (supports wildcards like 'branch-*').
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-query TEXT
Filter devices by a Lucene query.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-limit INTEGER RANGE
Maximum records to return  [default: 50; 1<=x<=200]
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-offset INTEGER RANGE
Pagination offset  [default: 0; x>=0]
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-device\-uids TEXT
List of device UIDs to add the shun on.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-ip\fP TEXT
Source IP to block. Repeat to shun multiple IPs in one transaction. Each value may embed a full connection tuple: '<src_ip> [<dst_ip> [<src_port> [<dst_port> [<protocol>]]]]'.  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-dest\-ip\fP TEXT
Destination IP of a specific connection to drop immediately. Only valid when a single --source-ip is given without an inline tuple.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-port\fP INTEGER
Source port of the connection to drop (requires --dest-ip).
.TP
\fB\-\-dest\-port\fP INTEGER
Destination port of the connection to drop (requires --dest-ip).
.TP
\fB\-\-protocol\fP [tcp|udp]
Protocol of the connection to drop (requires --dest-ip).
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without performing the operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fP / \-\-no\-wait
Wait for the transaction to finish before returning.  [default: no-wait]
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
